  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen the protection measures in Kaziranga and Manas National Park through advanced patrolling as a part of the program Indian Rhino Vision 2020 Phase-II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to help better manage the Protected Areas of Assam. Project objectives are as follows: (1) Establish best practice systems that can improve the effective use of information for conservation and monitoring; (2) The development and use of standardized processes together with flexibility to meet the different needs of the protected areas guidelines for data collection, analysis, and presentation that will promote meaningful assessment and enable comparability of conservation data across information management systems; (3) Develop suitable forms of spatial monitoring and recording tools to meet the management needs of protected area of Assam; and (4) Improve security in Kaziranga NP and Manas NP through improvised patrolling and monitoring, and continue support to run the existing Spatial Monitoring And Reporting Tool (SMART) patrolling in both the parks.</narrative>
  </description>
